    <string name="tweaks_mtk_title">MediaTek Engine</string>
    <string name="tweaks_mtk_info_title">Profile Information</string>
    <string name="tweaks_mtk_info_desc">FPSGO is a MediaTek kernel module that dynamically regulates CPU/GPU clocks based on real-time frame rate. When FPS is stable, clocks are lowered to save power — but in heavy scenes, this limitation can cause frame drops.

Features on this page are only active when the system is in the Performance profile. In Balanced or Eco profiles, the subsystem reverts to the standard baseline.</string>
    <string name="tweaks_fpsgo_title">Bypass Frame Limiter (FPSGo)</string>
    <string name="tweaks_fpsgo_desc">Disable FPSGO regulation so CPU/GPU clocks can rise freely as needed for rendering, without being capped when FPS seems stable. Higher power consumption and temperature.</string>
    <string name="tweaks_ged_title">Mali GED GPU Boost</string>
    <string name="tweaks_ged_desc">Send proactive boost signals to the Mali GPU via Graphics Event Daemon when render load spikes are detected, reducing frame drops before bottlenecks occur.</string>
